Known-deviation mismatch events: 1,051
     959 intentional-noise: The record is an intentionally corrupted OCR/telegraph transcription, so it cannot reproduce clean encryption or decryption exactly.
       6 historical-variant-navajo: The historical phrase uses the full USMC Navajo vocabulary and tokenization; the demo contains a small vocabulary subset.
       4 historical-variant-stager: The historical Stager record uses a specific route layout not represented by the demo column-count API.
       4 historical-variant-confederateVigenere: The historical brass-disk record uses a period alphabet/tableau; the demo implements ordinary repeating-key Vigenere.
       4 historical-variant-zimmermann: The historical telegram uses German diplomatic codebooks 0075/13040; the demo uses an illustrative English word list.
       4 historical-variant-vic: The historical VIC records require exact personal number, date, phrase, and transposition-width settings; the demo derives all four stages from one keyword.
       4 historical-variant-culperRing: The historical record uses original Tallmadge codebook numbers; the demo ships a smaller reconstructed codebook.
       4 historical-variant-vigenere: The historical record uses a period tableau/key convention that differs from the demo A-Z Vigenere convention.
       4 historical-variant-enigma: The historical record requires rotor order, rings, reflector, and plugboard settings unsupported by the simplified registry API; the full exhibit engine supports them.
       4 historical-variant-purple: The historical Purple record requires sixes/twenties switch wirings and stepping settings; the demo uses seeded substitution alphabets.
       4 historical-variant-babington: The historical Babington symbols and nomenclator are not the seeded bracket-token representation used by the demo.
       4 historical-variant-nullCipher: The historical record supplies an existing carrier text; the demo API instead generates its own carrier words from plaintext.
       4 historical-variant-kryptos: The historical Kryptos record uses sculpture-specific tableau and section conventions beyond the demo keyword-only model.
       2 historical-variant-alberti: The historical De Cifris record specifies disk alphabets and indicators not accepted by the demo numeric-setting API.
       2 historical-variant-adfgvx: The historical ADFGVX record uses a specific keyed 6x6 square and transposition convention not encoded in the demo key.
       2 historical-variant-lorenz: The historical Tunny record requires the actual SZ40/42 wheel patterns and settings; the demo derives illustrative wheel bits from a seed.
       2 historical-variant-sigaba: The historical SIGABA record requires real cipher/control/index rotor settings; the registry engine is a seeded pedagogical model.
       2 historical-variant-jefferson: The historical wheel record uses a specific physical disk alphabet/order set not present in the demo disk table.
       2 historical-variant-m94: The historical M-94 record uses issued disk alphabets and order; the registry engine generates seeded illustrative disks.
       2 historical-variant-bookCipher: The historical record is the unsolved Beale Paper No. 1; its true plaintext and key text are unknown, so no engine can reproduce it.
       2 historical-variant-greatCipher: The historical Grand Chiffre record uses the Rossignol numerical codebook; the demo has an illustrative syllable table.
       2 historical-variant-venonaPadReuse: The historical VENONA record uses Soviet five-digit code groups and additive pads; the demo is a simplified A-Z 5-bit XOR model.
       2 historical-variant-arnoldAndre: The historical book references depend on the exact Blackstone edition and page layout; the demo uses a reconstructed 240-word source.
       2 historical-variant-diana: The historical Diana record uses published pad-group conventions not represented by the demo keyword-only API.
       2 historical-variant-m209: The historical M-209 record requires explicit wheel pins, lugs, and starting positions; the demo derives all state from one seed.
       2 historical-variant-jn25: The historical JN-25 record requires the operational codebook and additive tables; the demo maps individual letters to invented groups.
       2 historical-variant-geheimschreiber: The historical T52 record uses Baudot and actual wheel/permutation settings; the demo is an A-Z seeded structural model.
       2 historical-variant-kl7: The historical KL-7 record requires real rotor, ring, notch, and re-entry settings; the demo derives illustrative state from one seed.
       2 historical-variant-fialka: The historical Fialka record uses a 30-character alphabet and real rotor settings; the demo uses a seeded 26-letter model.
       2 historical-variant-chaocipher: The historical Chaocipher record specifies independent left and right alphabets; the demo derives both from one keyword.
       2 historical-variant-wallisCiphers: The historical Wallis record uses its original intercepted nomenclator; the demo uses a small reconstructed word list.
       2 historical-variant-chineseTelegraph: The historical Chinese Telegraph record maps Chinese characters through the standard codebook; the demo maps Latin A-Z to illustrative groups.
       2 historical-variant-wheatstone: The historical Wheatstone record requires explicit inner/outer disk alphabets and start positions; the demo accepts only a keyword.
       2 historical-variant-copiale: The historical Copiale record uses manuscript glyphs and the recovered homophonic mapping; the demo uses synthetic letter-digit symbols.
